-- What PoliteLang can do with numbers.

-- The four everyday ones, in words or in symbols. Both mean the same thing.
please show 7 plus 3
please show 7 + 3
please show 7 minus 3
please show 7 times 3
please show 7 divided by 2 or 0

-- Dividing might not work out, because nothing can be shared into zero parts.
please show 7 divided by 0 or 0
please show the remainder of 17 divided by 5 or 0

-- Powers and roots.
please show 2 to the power of 10
please show the square root of 144 or 0
please show the square root of 0 minus 4 or 0

-- Rounding, three ways.
please show the rounded version of 3.6
please show the rounded down version of 3.9
please show the rounded up version of 3.1

-- Comparing, and picking.
please show the smaller of 12 and 7
please show the larger of 12 and 7
please show the size of 0 minus 9
please show 15 divides evenly by 5

-- Whole and decimal numbers mix freely, and mixing gives a decimal.
please show 1 plus 0.5
please show 10 divided by 4 or 0

-- Working on a whole list of numbers at once.
please remember scores is an empty list
please for every n in the pieces of "88 74 91 63 100" split by " ":
    add the number in n or 0 to scores
thank you for repeating

please show "there are {the number of items in scores} scores"
please show "they add up to {the total of scores}"
please show "the average is {the average of scores or 0}"
please show "the best is {the biggest of scores or 0}"
please show "the worst is {the smallest of scores or 0}"
please show "in order: {the join of the sorted version of scores with ", "}"

-- Building something up, the way you would on paper.
please define add up to with a limit:
    remember total is 0
    repeat for every n from 1 to limit:
        add n to total
    thanks
    give back total
thank you for defining

please show "1 to 100 adds up to {add up to with 100}"

-- Enough arithmetic to be dangerous: is a number prime?
please define is prime with a number:
    check if number is under 2:
        give back no
    thanks
    remember divisor is 2
    repeat while divisor times divisor is at most number:
        check if number divides evenly by divisor:
            give back no
        thanks
        add 1 to divisor
    thanks
    give back yes
thank you for defining

please remember primes is an empty list
please repeat for every n from 1 to 40:
    check if is prime with n:
        add n to primes
    thanks
thanks

please show "primes under 40: {the join of primes with ", "}"

-- And chance, when you want it.
please show a random whole number from 1 to 6
